1
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,780
Do we really have to break up?

2
00:00:51,103 --> 00:00:52,660
I don't want to do long-distance.

3
00:01:00,932 --> 00:01:02,252
There's a blank space right here.

4
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:08,101
Sign it.

5
00:01:19,220 --> 00:01:23,421
[Good luck at your new place,
Blue. Love you forever.]

6
00:01:27,532 --> 00:01:28,533
I gotta go.

7
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:40,540
- Thank you.
- Hey, Blue.

8
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:41,870
Welcome.

9
00:02:45,292 --> 00:02:46,380
Oh, I missed you so much.

10
00:02:46,428 --> 00:02:48,700
How are you? How are you parents?

11
00:02:49,735 --> 00:02:50,860
They're doing well.

12
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,600
Let me help you with that.

13
00:02:54,263 --> 00:02:55,623
Whose fruit basket is this, Uncle?

14
00:02:56,236 --> 00:02:58,020
Oh, it's a customer's basket.

15
00:02:58,124 --> 00:03:00,260
I'm delivering it for your dad.

16
00:03:04,666 --> 00:03:05,667
Got it.

17
00:03:11,837 --> 00:03:14,460
- Is this everything you packed?
- Yeah.

18
00:03:14,900 --> 00:03:15,901
Let's go.

19
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,001
You should go now.

20
00:03:21,012 --> 00:03:22,180
I'll see you off here.

21
00:03:22,882 --> 00:03:25,300
Take good care of yourself, Blue.

22
00:03:26,500 --> 00:03:27,501
Thank you,

23
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:30,100
and please tell Mom and Dad not to worry.

24
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:34,501
Let's go.

25
00:03:37,501 --> 00:03:38,981
I'll show you around your new school.

26
00:03:42,263 --> 00:03:43,264
It's there?

27
00:03:43,351 --> 00:03:45,020
Yeah, just go straight.

28
00:03:47,365 --> 00:03:48,366
I see the sign.

29
00:03:56,306 --> 00:03:57,307
Hey!

30
00:03:57,980 --> 00:03:59,380
Isn't the dorm this way?

31
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:02,780
Yeah, but we're going somewhere else first.

32
00:04:05,679 --> 00:04:07,820
You go on. I can find the dorm myself.

33
00:04:09,644 --> 00:04:10,645
I flunked my exams,

34
00:04:11,192 --> 00:04:13,740
so I have to do community
service for the school.

35
00:04:14,012 --> 00:04:17,180
They need two people,
and I already signed you up.

36
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:19,141
Help me out,

37
00:04:19,346 --> 00:04:21,600
and you can have the bottom bunk.

38
00:04:21,655 --> 00:04:22,656
Please, Blue. Please?

39
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:45,740
[Chantrawattana School
Foundation Annual Charity Fair]

40
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:51,501
Dorm kids are basically their servants,

41
00:04:52,082 --> 00:04:54,402
if they want dorm points anyway.
Think of this as practice.

42
00:04:56,071 --> 00:04:58,860
And your parents are okay with you
moving to another province?

43
00:05:00,983 --> 00:05:02,904
Mom didn't really want me to move here,

44
00:05:04,764 --> 00:05:06,940
but when I brought up college,

45
00:05:07,671 --> 00:05:08,791
she couldn't exactly say no.

46
00:05:10,594 --> 00:05:11,900
And my dad…

47
00:05:14,028 --> 00:05:16,260
I don't know. I guess Mom told him.

48
00:05:41,532 --> 00:05:43,900
Good evening, Mr. Po and Mr. Yi.

49
00:05:44,076 --> 00:05:45,077
Good evening, Director.

50
00:05:45,474 --> 00:05:47,580
I'm sorry I'm late.

51
00:05:47,938 --> 00:05:50,700
You're not late at all.
You arrived just in time.

52
00:05:50,812 --> 00:05:53,100
Tokyo is about to perform.

53
00:05:53,623 --> 00:05:55,624
Why don't you come sit at the table first?

54
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,061
Please follow me.

55
00:06:04,631 --> 00:06:07,100
Pupe, I told you to go left! Hurry up!

56
00:06:07,266 --> 00:06:08,820
Well, I am!

57
00:06:11,532 --> 00:06:14,740
Tokyo, you're up next, okay?
Your dad's waiting to see you perform.

58
00:06:16,271 --> 00:06:17,272
Okay, ma'am.

59
00:06:22,330 --> 00:06:23,331
Damn it!

60
00:06:23,743 --> 00:06:24,744
That wasn't the cue.

61
00:06:25,094 --> 00:06:26,260
Make your move now.

62
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:55,621
[Singing off-key.]

63
00:07:12,775 --> 00:07:15,380
Tokyo's voice sounds
really good today, Mr. Po.

64
00:07:16,119 --> 00:07:17,500
Sounds good, my ass.

65
00:07:18,658 --> 00:07:19,659
Blue, come on.

66
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:21,500
Don't give in to the voice in your head.

67
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:23,220
Keep your thoughts to yourself.

68
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:26,740
That's Tokyo, one of the Street Queens.
Her dad's a big shot around here.

69
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:28,850
That guy is Mr. Po,

70
00:07:29,314 --> 00:07:30,315
her dad.

71
00:07:42,060 --> 00:07:44,380
Go handle it. Don't embarrass us.

72
00:07:45,226 --> 00:07:46,227
Yes, Dad.

73
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:05,741
Hurry up.

74
00:08:11,564 --> 00:08:12,565
Where the hell is she?

75
00:08:13,218 --> 00:08:14,860
Split up! Don't let Tokyo escape!

76
00:08:23,490 --> 00:08:24,491
Hey, you.

77
00:08:25,660 --> 00:08:27,060
Could you go to the school entrance

78
00:08:27,119 --> 00:08:29,340
and pick up the birthday
cake for the guest?

79
00:08:29,722 --> 00:08:30,882
Bring it inside for me, okay?

80
00:08:31,162 --> 00:08:32,163
I can help her.

81
00:08:32,335 --> 00:08:34,420
No need to. The new girl can handle this.

82
00:08:35,754 --> 00:08:36,906
Come on, you're coming with me.

83
00:08:36,930 --> 00:08:39,060
We need your help over there. Let's go.

84
00:08:41,623 --> 00:08:42,624
Hold on.

85
00:08:45,804 --> 00:08:46,805
Is Tokyo inside?

86
00:08:51,452 --> 00:08:52,852
Are you two running away like this?

87
00:08:53,004 --> 00:08:54,100
No, Yi. I'm just…

88
00:08:54,300 --> 00:08:56,500
I'm taking the cart to
get water for the guests.

89
00:08:56,986 --> 00:08:57,987
Oh, really?

90
00:08:58,220 --> 00:08:59,221
Move, kid.

91
00:09:20,100 --> 00:09:21,501
[With the utmost respect.]

92
00:09:38,431 --> 00:09:39,432
Hey!

93
00:09:42,842 --> 00:09:43,843
Shit!

94
00:10:12,978 --> 00:10:14,660
Am I screwed from day one?

95
00:10:23,950 --> 00:10:25,230
Are you even going to apologize?

96
00:10:26,556 --> 00:10:28,540
Apologize for what? You ran into me.

97
00:10:28,967 --> 00:10:29,968
What?

98
00:10:30,098 --> 00:10:31,658
That's a pretty messed-up thing to say.

99
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:32,941
I know.

100
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:34,860
People called me pretty all the time.

101
00:10:35,954 --> 00:10:37,794
Can't you just say sorry
like a normal person?

102
00:10:38,098 --> 00:10:39,298
Do you have to be such a jerk?

103
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:42,141
Hey, ladies!

104
00:10:44,202 --> 00:10:45,500
I didn't do it.

105
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:50,061
Follow me.

106
00:10:52,876 --> 00:10:53,877
Okay.

107
00:11:09,900 --> 00:11:11,901
[Singing]

108
00:11:31,847 --> 00:11:32,848
Mr. Po.

109
00:11:33,911 --> 00:11:37,340
A student dropped Chief Tul's cake, sir.

110
00:11:41,058 --> 00:11:42,059
Good evening.

111
00:11:44,756 --> 00:11:45,757
Oh, hello.

112
00:11:52,887 --> 00:11:54,140
Good evening, sir.

113
00:11:54,802 --> 00:11:55,803
Good evening.

114
00:11:56,580 --> 00:11:57,581
Hope you're doing well.

115
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:04,020
[With the deepest respect,
Wiboon Monchaitrakul]

116
00:12:08,098 --> 00:12:09,099
Oh,

117
00:12:09,620 --> 00:12:12,780
someone dropped by with
a gift to congratulate me.

118
00:12:12,927 --> 00:12:13,928
I see.

119
00:12:15,407 --> 00:12:17,460
Actually, I still have many gifts for you,

120
00:12:17,714 --> 00:12:20,820
but they're currently on
their way from Singapore.

121
00:12:21,820 --> 00:12:24,180
Once my other son returns to Thailand,

122
00:12:24,359 --> 00:12:26,420
I assure you they'll be
delivered straight to you.

123
00:12:27,394 --> 00:12:30,660
I hope we can continue
to count on your kindness.

124
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:32,621
Thank you.

125
00:12:36,580 --> 00:12:37,860
You know me so well.

126
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:41,661
This way, please.

127
00:12:46,290 --> 00:12:47,400
Is that your daughter?

128
00:12:47,935 --> 00:12:48,940
That's right.

129
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:51,701
She has a great voice.

130
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:52,939
Thank you, sir.

131
00:13:02,316 --> 00:13:03,756
You need to soak your clothes first.

132
00:13:05,148 --> 00:13:06,220
Blue!

133
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:07,988
You're only supposed to add one scoop.

134
00:13:08,012 --> 00:13:10,572
Are you planning to get these clothes clean
by next year or what?

135
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:13,100
Yeah, I'll wash all this bad
luck away once and for all.

136
00:13:14,375 --> 00:13:16,820
I warned you not to mess with Tokyo.

137
00:13:17,724 --> 00:13:19,200
I wasn't trying to mess with her.

138
00:13:20,172 --> 00:13:21,420
She bumped into me.

139
00:13:23,652 --> 00:13:26,463
And what the hell is wrong
with the teachers here?

140
00:13:28,623 --> 00:13:30,583
They don't even punish
the person who started it.

141
00:13:31,780 --> 00:13:34,781
Every teacher in this school is obviously
taking Tokyo's side.

142
00:13:35,055 --> 00:13:36,455
Because her last name is Kongpurim.

143
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:39,141
Look over there.

144
00:13:39,988 --> 00:13:41,028
That's Mr. Po's real name.

145
00:13:42,738 --> 00:13:44,338
Are we still dealing with social status?

146
00:13:45,292 --> 00:13:46,932
People are supposed to be equal nowadays.

147
00:13:47,623 --> 00:13:48,780
Equal, huh?

148
00:13:50,860 --> 00:13:52,220
They just have more money than us.

149
00:13:57,636 --> 00:14:00,042
I've got money too. Why should I back down?

150
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:02,781
This school belongs to Tokyo.

151
00:14:14,708 --> 00:14:15,860
Who's part of this crew?

152
00:14:39,266 --> 00:14:41,460
I heard there's a new girl. Who is she?

153
00:14:41,687 --> 00:14:44,580
You'll know soon. Someone is already
giving her a proper welcome.

154
00:14:46,895 --> 00:14:48,420
Go ahead and leave your phone here.

155
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:50,781
Then you can introduce
yourself to everyone.

156
00:14:57,860 --> 00:14:58,861
Hello, everyone.

157
00:14:59,140 --> 00:15:00,141
My name is Blue,

158
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:02,140
Phakjira Monchaitrakul.

159
00:15:07,503 --> 00:15:10,140
Once you've introduced yourself,
take the desk in the back.

160
00:15:11,700 --> 00:15:12,701
Right there.

161
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:13,901
Hey, everyone.

162
00:15:14,178 --> 00:15:16,620
Finish your homework, okay?
I'll come back and check it later.

163
00:15:22,780 --> 00:15:24,140
You're in my seat. Move.

164
00:15:25,786 --> 00:15:26,900
And this one is mine.

165
00:15:30,666 --> 00:15:33,780
Oh, so you're Zai and Pupe.

166
00:15:35,084 --> 00:15:36,782
Tokyo's lapdogs.

167
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:39,020
There is no reason to be rude.

168
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:40,700
Are you trying to pick a fight with me?

169
00:15:42,636 --> 00:15:45,180
Didn't your parents teach you any manners?

170
00:15:46,236 --> 00:15:47,237
They did.

171
00:15:47,714 --> 00:15:49,914
They taught me to save them
for people who deserve them.

172
00:15:52,242 --> 00:15:54,282
You two went through my
bag last night, didn't you?

173
00:15:54,668 --> 00:15:55,951
I don't know what you're talking about.

174
00:15:55,975 --> 00:15:57,780
What are you talking
about? We didn't do it.

175
00:15:58,988 --> 00:16:00,220
You did it, so own up to it.

176
00:16:00,295 --> 00:16:02,620
I told you I didn't do it.
What's wrong with you?

177
00:16:16,914 --> 00:16:17,915
Hey!

178
00:16:20,439 --> 00:16:21,440
What the hell?

179
00:16:32,988 --> 00:16:33,989
Oh,

180
00:16:35,292 --> 00:16:36,293
it's you.

181
00:16:37,607 --> 00:16:39,287
You're new here, at least you should learn

182
00:16:40,114 --> 00:16:41,400
how things are done around here.

183
00:16:42,236 --> 00:16:43,237
Why?

184
00:16:43,460 --> 00:16:45,860
Since when do you have to
be a gangster just to sit in class?

185
00:16:46,506 --> 00:16:48,140
- A gangster?
- I'm talking about you?

186
00:16:50,127 --> 00:16:51,460
You know me that well, huh?

187
00:16:51,980 --> 00:16:53,180
Enough to call me a gangster?

188
00:16:54,849 --> 00:16:56,969
You've got your name
plastered all over the building.

189
00:16:57,412 --> 00:16:58,932
You'd have to be an idiot not to know.

190
00:17:01,513 --> 00:17:03,060
I heard your dad's such a big shot?

191
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:07,340
Don't forget, he's not
the one sitting in class.

192
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:13,060
Where am I allowed to sit?

193
00:17:15,220 --> 00:17:16,580
Sit wherever you want.

194
00:17:17,223 --> 00:17:18,660
There are plenty of empty seats.

195
00:17:19,292 --> 00:17:21,140
Just don't sit in someone else's seat.

196
00:17:21,191 --> 00:17:22,192
Yeah?

197
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:24,580
So, does that mean I can sit on your head?

198
00:17:28,234 --> 00:17:29,474
Can you stop being a smart-ass?

199
00:17:29,660 --> 00:17:31,661
I told you, sit wherever you want,

200
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:34,300
as long as it's not someone else's seat.

201
00:17:37,850 --> 00:17:40,260
Holy shit, someone's
actually standing up to Tokyo.

202
00:17:44,748 --> 00:17:45,749
Hey!

203
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:47,980
What is going on over there?

204
00:17:50,420 --> 00:17:53,420
Phakjira, you still haven't found a seat?

205
00:17:54,050 --> 00:17:56,660
I told you to sit over
there, next to Zai's desk.

206
00:18:01,444 --> 00:18:04,060
Nice. Making trouble
on your first day already.

207
00:18:04,751 --> 00:18:05,823
I didn't start it.

208
00:18:05,836 --> 00:18:06,937
You're still talking back?

209
00:18:19,252 --> 00:18:20,253
Tokyo, dear.

210
00:18:21,092 --> 00:18:23,852
The English literature board in
the library isn't finished yet, is it?

211
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:27,341
I think I've found
someone to do it for you.

212
00:19:06,516 --> 00:19:07,663
Hello, Captain Big.

213
00:19:07,812 --> 00:19:10,060
Hello, were you here to see my dad?

214
00:19:10,146 --> 00:19:12,140
I thought I'd stop by for some good luck
before I go gambling today.

215
00:19:12,164 --> 00:19:14,340
Hopefully, luck will be on my side.

216
00:19:14,740 --> 00:19:15,741
- I should go.
- Okay.

217
00:19:28,231 --> 00:19:29,500
How was your trip to Singapore?

218
00:19:29,863 --> 00:19:30,864
It was nice.

219
00:19:38,932 --> 00:19:40,612
We made it just in time to submit our bid.

220
00:19:41,218 --> 00:19:42,780
These are just the backup ones, Dad.

221
00:19:43,543 --> 00:19:46,223
I already gave the main batch to
Chief Tul's men before I came home.

222
00:19:49,746 --> 00:19:52,586
We managed to pull the money
from the Singapore account first this time,

223
00:19:56,108 --> 00:19:57,740
but if we let Yi keep operating it,

224
00:19:59,796 --> 00:20:01,836
the numbers will keep
sinking further into the red.

225
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:05,413
Big, you ass hole.

226
00:20:05,442 --> 00:20:06,660
You're a captain, for crying out loud.

227
00:20:06,684 --> 00:20:08,204
Can't you handle something this small?

228
00:20:08,908 --> 00:20:10,783
Are you letting patrol cops
raid the gambling den every day?

229
00:20:10,807 --> 00:20:12,287
How am I supposed to make any profit?

230
00:20:12,748 --> 00:20:14,150
Fuck, I'm already handling it.

231
00:20:15,244 --> 00:20:18,524
Those guys are just doing a routine inspection
to keep the locals from complaining.

232
00:20:19,666 --> 00:20:21,466
The gambling den isn't
what's losing money...

233
00:20:22,759 --> 00:20:24,879
our family's going under
because of your boxing camp.

234
00:20:25,266 --> 00:20:27,066
You're always paying for
everything for your men.

235
00:20:28,556 --> 00:20:29,980
Yi made the right call.

236
00:20:31,484 --> 00:20:33,220
The boxing camp is there to support my men.

237
00:20:34,188 --> 00:20:35,989
And when you run in the next election,

238
00:20:37,234 --> 00:20:40,060
you'll be relying on all these people to
act as your vote canvassers.

239
00:20:41,479 --> 00:20:42,480
Dad,

240
00:20:43,367 --> 00:20:45,247
I can quit and help with
the family's business.

241
00:20:46,415 --> 00:20:47,416
No need to.

242
00:20:48,431 --> 00:20:49,740
Yi can handle everything.

243
00:20:51,263 --> 00:20:53,500
I've planned everything out for you.

244
00:20:54,204 --> 00:20:55,820
All you have to do is follow the plan.

245
00:20:58,714 --> 00:20:59,715
Dad?

246
00:21:01,135 --> 00:21:02,700
Did you plan everything out for Tokyo?

247
00:21:03,780 --> 00:21:06,060
Let's worry about getting her
to wake up for school first.

248
00:21:08,340 --> 00:21:09,600
Can't you two even take care

249
00:21:10,439 --> 00:21:11,660
of your little sister?

250
00:21:22,375 --> 00:21:23,376
Yes, Uncle.

251
00:21:26,247 --> 00:21:27,248
Got it.

252
00:21:29,892 --> 00:21:30,900
What's the matter?

253
00:21:32,868 --> 00:21:35,108
Somboon said there was a problem
with the bid submission.

254
00:21:43,999 --> 00:21:45,460
A new bidder competed against us

255
00:21:46,420 --> 00:21:47,460
and they got the contract.

256
00:21:48,490 --> 00:21:49,491
Who's that?

257
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:53,061
It's Monchaitrakul.

258
00:22:25,074 --> 00:22:28,060
Ms. Paew from Class 6/3 sent me to help
with the bulletin board.

259
00:22:28,396 --> 00:22:29,900
Oh, you're the new girl.

260
00:22:30,119 --> 00:22:31,580
Ms. Paew told me about you.

261
00:22:31,879 --> 00:22:34,940
Nothing much. You can just
decorate the library bulletin board.

262
00:22:35,511 --> 00:22:39,020
The topic can be anything
related to classic literature.

263
00:22:39,703 --> 00:22:42,820
You can find the materials yourself—
whatever works for you.

264
00:22:51,324 --> 00:22:52,325
What?

265
00:22:52,610 --> 00:22:54,076
Why are you still here?

266
00:22:54,327 --> 00:22:57,127
You've got just three days to
put the bulletin board together, sweetie.

267
00:22:57,399 --> 00:22:58,400
Three days.

268
00:22:58,450 --> 00:22:59,451
Move along.

269
00:23:45,284 --> 00:23:46,420
You scared me!

270
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:49,140
Can't you just come in properly?

271
00:23:50,780 --> 00:23:52,420
There's one left, I haven't...

272
00:26:54,500 --> 00:26:56,660
[Throw this away for me. I have to run.]

273
00:27:00,201 --> 00:27:01,202
Bitch.

274
00:27:11,380 --> 00:27:12,785
Ms. Tokyo, you can park here.

275
00:27:12,916 --> 00:27:14,700
It's okay. I can park in the back.

276
00:27:29,943 --> 00:27:30,944
See?

277
00:27:31,180 --> 00:27:32,900
I'm not some gangster like you assumed.

278
00:27:36,615 --> 00:27:38,860
Yeah? What is that?

279
00:27:53,940 --> 00:27:56,420
[Love until our last breath]

280
00:28:06,839 --> 00:28:09,440
[Willing to die for love]

281
00:28:25,988 --> 00:28:26,989
So cringe.

282
00:28:28,215 --> 00:28:29,740
Who the hell would die for love?

283
00:28:33,100 --> 00:28:34,301
They call it a classic.

284
00:28:39,154 --> 00:28:40,380
Can you help...

285
00:28:52,324 --> 00:28:53,325
Hey.

286
00:28:53,658 --> 00:28:55,338
If you're going to come here and not help,

287
00:28:55,812 --> 00:28:57,012
don't bother coming next time.

288
00:29:03,983 --> 00:29:05,260
You can't fool me twice.

289
00:29:06,239 --> 00:29:07,300
You think I'm that stupid?

290
00:29:10,020 --> 00:29:11,183
This isn't trash.

291
00:29:12,340 --> 00:29:13,341
I brought you some chips.

292
00:29:49,708 --> 00:29:52,551
Ju... Julite?

293
00:29:52,772 --> 00:29:55,180
It's spelled J-U-L-I-E-T, not J-U-L-I-T-E.

294
00:29:56,967 --> 00:29:57,980
Did you type that wrong?

295
00:30:05,820 --> 00:30:06,821
Hey!

296
00:30:09,428 --> 00:30:10,429
It's Juliet.

297
00:30:28,919 --> 00:30:30,119
Your drawings are really good.

298
00:30:31,300 --> 00:30:32,701
Do you ever take commissions?

299
00:30:33,778 --> 00:30:34,779
Nope.

300
00:30:35,490 --> 00:30:36,500
They're for my eyes only.

301
00:30:38,010 --> 00:30:39,420
What? What do you mean?

302
00:30:39,647 --> 00:30:42,647
Your skills are good enough to compete
with artists from all over the world.

303
00:30:47,700 --> 00:30:48,701
- Hey.
- Hey.

304
00:30:51,431 --> 00:30:53,220
Why are you talking to me?
What do you want?

305
00:30:54,042 --> 00:30:56,042
You're already listed as
part of the group anyway.

306
00:30:56,735 --> 00:30:58,060
I saw you working alone,

307
00:30:59,180 --> 00:31:00,580
so I came over to keep you company.

308
00:31:01,911 --> 00:31:03,020
I don't want your company.

309
00:31:07,060 --> 00:31:08,600
I don't want to be part of a group…

310
00:31:09,061 --> 00:31:11,140
with a lame-ass name like “Street Queens.”

311
00:31:11,586 --> 00:31:12,587
What?

312
00:31:16,071 --> 00:31:17,072
What's the name again?

313
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:18,501
Street Queens, isn't it?

314
00:31:22,780 --> 00:31:23,781
Are you insane?

315
00:31:24,980 --> 00:31:26,660
Who would call themselves “Street Queens”?

316
00:31:27,999 --> 00:31:30,740
We didn't name ourselves
that. Our classmates did.

317
00:31:31,500 --> 00:31:32,540
Street Queens, really?

318
00:31:39,436 --> 00:31:40,437
Hey,

319
00:31:42,180 --> 00:31:43,260
are you still mad?

320
00:31:47,695 --> 00:31:50,135
About what you said about
someone going through your things...

321
00:31:50,362 --> 00:31:52,140
we didn't do it.

322
00:31:53,794 --> 00:31:54,914
The same goes for the seats.

323
00:31:55,170 --> 00:31:57,300
Those seats really
belonged to Zai and Pupe.

324
00:31:58,402 --> 00:31:59,420
We didn't do it.

325
00:32:00,828 --> 00:32:02,180
About the classmates,

326
00:32:04,306 --> 00:32:05,780
you transferred here in 12th grade,

327
00:32:07,207 --> 00:32:08,540
so they're probably just curious.

328
00:32:09,415 --> 00:32:10,580
You showed up out of nowhere.

329
00:32:11,762 --> 00:32:13,260
You could've just asked

330
00:32:14,180 --> 00:32:15,460
instead of bullying someone

331
00:32:15,631 --> 00:32:17,220
and expecting them to treat you well.

332
00:32:22,650 --> 00:32:25,200
I transferred here to apply through the
art program's quota.

333
00:32:43,860 --> 00:32:46,380
Why didn't you use the bandage I gave you?

334
00:32:48,450 --> 00:32:49,500
Oh, it's nothing.

335
00:32:52,018 --> 00:32:53,019
It's not nothing.

336
00:32:56,482 --> 00:32:57,483
Turn and face me.

337
00:34:05,898 --> 00:34:06,899
What?

338
00:34:07,623 --> 00:34:09,180
DaouOffroad will be here?

339
00:34:10,100 --> 00:34:12,101
Let me see.

340
00:34:15,183 --> 00:34:16,500
It's not far from here.

341
00:34:17,660 --> 00:34:18,661
We should go.

342
00:34:20,748 --> 00:34:21,780
How could we go?

343
00:34:22,697 --> 00:34:24,417
I'm not allowed to leave the dorm at night.

344
00:34:25,945 --> 00:34:26,950
Of course, you can.

345
00:34:27,780 --> 00:34:28,781
You can just walk.

346
00:34:30,591 --> 00:34:31,592
Look,

347
00:34:31,834 --> 00:34:33,340
I'm not some big shot like you.

348
00:34:34,230 --> 00:34:36,550
I can't just go wherever
I want without getting in trouble.

349
00:34:54,676 --> 00:34:55,677
Get up.

350
00:34:56,600 --> 00:34:58,520
Where are we going?
The work isn't finished yet.

351
00:34:59,300 --> 00:35:00,700
To go see your favorite duo.

352
00:35:05,420 --> 00:35:06,500
You're with the big shot.

353
00:35:07,020 --> 00:35:08,140
No one's gonna say anything.

354
00:35:22,935 --> 00:35:24,100
Aren't you the big shot?

355
00:35:24,780 --> 00:35:26,650
Why can't we just get me
out through the front gate?

356
00:35:26,674 --> 00:35:27,700
Actually, we can.

357
00:35:28,535 --> 00:35:30,700
But I don't want my dad's
guys to know where I am.

358
00:35:31,074 --> 00:35:32,075
I don't like it.

359
00:35:32,940 --> 00:35:34,660
Nepo baby, for real.

360
00:35:41,714 --> 00:35:43,060
- Are you serious?
- Yeah.

361
00:35:46,644 --> 00:35:47,900
You go first.

362
00:35:48,586 --> 00:35:50,066
- Are you sure it's safe?
- Of course.

363
00:35:54,511 --> 00:35:55,512
Get up there.

364
00:36:07,524 --> 00:36:08,525
You good?

365
00:36:08,700 --> 00:36:09,701
- Yeah.
- Catch this.

366
00:36:13,524 --> 00:36:14,525
One more.

367
00:36:30,119 --> 00:36:31,540
Can we wear this inside?

368
00:36:31,948 --> 00:36:33,000
And we're still underage.

369
00:36:33,820 --> 00:36:35,050
Hello, Tokyo.

370
00:36:35,519 --> 00:36:37,060
Your brother is not here with you?

371
00:36:37,780 --> 00:36:38,781
I'm here with my friend.

372
00:36:39,482 --> 00:36:41,540
I'll have someone save two seats for you.

373
00:36:48,615 --> 00:36:50,420
Please put on your jackets.

374
00:37:08,962 --> 00:37:10,000
Are you alright?

375
00:37:11,620 --> 00:37:12,700
We're here now, aren't we?

376
00:37:13,420 --> 00:37:15,500
I wonder what it's like

377
00:37:15,521 --> 00:37:16,881
to live with powerful connections.

378
00:37:21,511 --> 00:37:22,512
Welcome.

379
00:37:58,335 --> 00:38:01,580
Wow, mob boss's daughters
still exist these days?

380
00:38:03,449 --> 00:38:04,450
They still exist.

381
00:38:05,284 --> 00:38:07,660
We just don't call them mob bosses anymore.

382
00:38:08,252 --> 00:38:10,380
These days, we call them…

383
00:38:11,015 --> 00:38:12,060
“powerful figures.”

384
00:38:13,447 --> 00:38:15,000
Whoa, powerful figures.

385
00:38:19,452 --> 00:38:20,572
What happened to that wound?

386
00:38:21,620 --> 00:38:23,420
Who did you get into a fight with?

387
00:38:25,559 --> 00:38:26,560
You mean this?

388
00:38:31,471 --> 00:38:32,500
I don't remember.

389
00:38:32,932 --> 00:38:34,200
You've been in a lot of fights.

390
00:38:36,740 --> 00:38:37,986
Yeah, quite a lot.

391
00:38:38,450 --> 00:38:40,620
But it's not what you think.

392
00:38:41,143 --> 00:38:42,144
Well…

393
00:38:42,754 --> 00:38:45,020
Dad said I was really
stubborn when I was younger.

394
00:38:45,399 --> 00:38:47,460
I used to wander around all the time,

395
00:38:48,180 --> 00:38:49,460
and then I fell down the stairs.

396
00:38:52,252 --> 00:38:54,260
Don't tell anyone.

397
00:38:54,583 --> 00:38:56,303
You'll lose you mob boss's daughter credit.

398
00:38:57,700 --> 00:38:58,900
I've never told anyone.

399
00:39:02,308 --> 00:39:05,050
I haven't done anything
as impressive as you think.

400
00:39:05,978 --> 00:39:07,540
I'm just a normal girl.

401
00:39:09,626 --> 00:39:10,627
Not true.

402
00:39:11,487 --> 00:39:14,140
At least, your family is wealthy.

403
00:39:15,476 --> 00:39:16,860
So, your name's Tokyo.

404
00:39:18,367 --> 00:39:19,500
Were you born in Tokyo?

405
00:39:22,314 --> 00:39:23,315
Nope.

406
00:39:26,490 --> 00:39:29,290
I was named after my dad's favorite snack,
a Thai treat called “Tokyo.”

407
00:39:35,020 --> 00:39:36,021
What's the filling?

408
00:39:37,231 --> 00:39:38,860
I don't know. You have to ask him.

409
00:39:39,092 --> 00:39:40,200
Nope.

410
00:39:41,140 --> 00:39:43,260
I asked you—what's the filling?

411
00:39:48,239 --> 00:39:49,240
What's the filling?

412
00:39:51,800 --> 00:39:53,380
Good... feelings.

413
00:39:58,116 --> 00:39:59,460
Fine. Good feelings it is.

414
00:40:01,946 --> 00:40:03,620
Which one do you recommend, local expert?

415
00:40:04,820 --> 00:40:06,260
I haven't tried them either.

416
00:40:07,977 --> 00:40:09,300
I'll get whatever you get.

417
00:40:11,428 --> 00:40:12,429
Hello.

418
00:40:16,010 --> 00:40:17,130
We'd like to order this one.

419
00:40:17,556 --> 00:40:18,557
You got it.

420
00:40:40,002 --> 00:40:41,003
You think it'd help?

421
00:41:14,634 --> 00:41:15,635
Cheers!

422
00:41:26,935 --> 00:41:28,175
Don't your mom and dad miss you

423
00:41:28,823 --> 00:41:30,220
after you moved here?

424
00:41:33,586 --> 00:41:34,587
Well…

425
00:41:34,924 --> 00:41:37,860
consider it practice for
college life in Bangkok.

426
00:41:41,314 --> 00:41:43,900
Are you that confident you'll get in?

427
00:41:44,156 --> 00:41:45,157
Wait,

428
00:41:46,237 --> 00:41:49,220
weren't you the one

429
00:41:49,730 --> 00:41:51,180
who said I draw well?

430
00:41:56,409 --> 00:41:57,900
Yes, I like your drawings.

431
00:41:59,695 --> 00:42:01,775
You're going to get in
through the art quota anyway.

432
00:42:02,620 --> 00:42:03,621
That's right.

433
00:42:04,340 --> 00:42:06,322
I will get in.

434
00:42:20,005 --> 00:42:23,180
♪ Hey, is the world ♪

435
00:42:23,220 --> 00:42:27,740
♪ still not hot enough for you? ♪

436
00:42:29,404 --> 00:42:32,420
♪ Everything you do ♪

437
00:42:32,636 --> 00:42:37,140
♪ just drives the temperature higher. ♪

438
00:42:37,415 --> 00:42:41,100
♪ Every move you make,
every look you give, ♪

439
00:42:41,191 --> 00:42:43,740
♪ drives me crazy. ♪

440
00:42:44,348 --> 00:42:48,940
♪ No matter how hard
I try, I can't resist you. ♪

441
00:42:53,780 --> 00:42:58,600
♪ The temperature of my
heart is out of control. ♪

442
00:43:00,938 --> 00:43:04,740
♪ You set me burning,
burning, burning inside— ♪

443
00:43:05,300 --> 00:43:07,200
♪ Teasing, till my heart melts. ♪

444
00:43:07,420 --> 00:43:09,750
♪ My heats is melting and melting. ♪

445
00:43:09,780 --> 00:43:12,500
♪ I'm ready for you to
burn my body and soul. ♪

446
00:43:17,930 --> 00:43:20,140
♪ You're melting my heart. ♪

447
00:43:21,480 --> 00:43:24,700
♪ My heats is melting and melting. ♪

448
00:43:27,340 --> 00:43:29,540
♪ You're melting my heart. ♪

449
00:43:35,383 --> 00:43:36,384
Hey!

450
00:43:47,831 --> 00:43:49,580
Oh, I threw up all over your shirt.

451
00:43:50,498 --> 00:43:52,380
- I'm sorry.
- It's okay.

452
00:43:52,817 --> 00:43:53,818
That's fine.

453
00:43:55,634 --> 00:43:56,635
It's a mess.

454
00:43:56,945 --> 00:43:59,340
It's totally fine. It's alright.

455
00:44:00,660 --> 00:44:01,661
Let's have a seat.

456
00:44:03,522 --> 00:44:05,140
Watch out! Walk slowly.

457
00:44:23,300 --> 00:44:25,420
Your name is Tokyo

458
00:44:26,175 --> 00:44:27,660
because you like to visit Japan?

459
00:44:29,814 --> 00:44:31,060
You asked me that already.

460
00:44:32,794 --> 00:44:34,354
I was named after Dad's favorite snack.

461
00:44:37,268 --> 00:44:38,500
That's so funny.

462
00:44:40,714 --> 00:44:41,874
What's your favorite filling?

463
00:44:43,540 --> 00:44:44,541
The sweet ones.

464
00:44:50,220 --> 00:44:51,260
I'll get some for you.

465
00:44:52,940 --> 00:44:53,941
What?

466
00:44:55,620 --> 00:44:57,500
- You're buying me snacks?
- Yeah.

467
00:45:00,743 --> 00:45:02,100
I want to pay you back.

468
00:45:06,124 --> 00:45:07,125
Yeah?

469
00:45:19,750 --> 00:45:20,751
Can I ask you something?

470
00:45:23,002 --> 00:45:24,003
What?

471
00:45:28,900 --> 00:45:30,001
Can we be friends now?

472
00:45:36,831 --> 00:45:37,832
Yeah.

473
00:45:46,663 --> 00:45:47,780
So we're friends now.

474
00:46:06,639 --> 00:46:07,640
Am I heavy?

475
00:46:07,920 --> 00:46:09,921
Of course you are. What
kind of question is that?

476
00:46:18,919 --> 00:46:20,839
Do I need to carry you
all the way to your room?

477
00:46:22,721 --> 00:46:23,722
You don't have to.

478
00:46:23,996 --> 00:46:25,820
Okay, I should go.

479
00:46:26,460 --> 00:46:27,461
See you tomorrow.

480
00:46:27,540 --> 00:46:29,300
Hey, hold on.

481
00:46:29,612 --> 00:46:30,613
What?

482
00:46:30,940 --> 00:46:31,941
Stay right here.

483
00:46:39,017 --> 00:46:40,018
What is it?

484
00:46:44,975 --> 00:46:46,775
Have you finished the
library bulletin board?

485
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:15,150
Actually, you don't have
to give me your shirt.

486
00:47:15,520 --> 00:47:16,740
[Sinittha Kongpurim]

487
00:47:16,834 --> 00:47:17,835
You can't.

488
00:47:18,100 --> 00:47:20,020
How can you wear it
when it's covered in my puke?

489
00:47:20,135 --> 00:47:21,140
Let me wash it first.

490
00:47:23,700 --> 00:47:24,701
Okay.

491
00:47:25,225 --> 00:47:26,985
Then make sure you
use fabric softener, too.

492
00:47:27,714 --> 00:47:28,820
I know.

493
00:47:29,831 --> 00:47:31,140
Alright, see you later.

494
00:47:31,388 --> 00:47:32,389
See ya.

495
00:47:47,002 --> 00:47:50,140
This is what happens to anyone

496
00:47:50,516 --> 00:47:52,756
who sells the Kongpurims'
information to the other side.

497
00:47:56,681 --> 00:47:59,340
Mr. Po, please. Give me another chance.

498
00:47:59,820 --> 00:48:01,780
You asked for another chance?

499
00:48:02,180 --> 00:48:03,181
I'm not giving it to you.

500
00:48:05,585 --> 00:48:06,586
Yi?

501
00:48:12,441 --> 00:48:13,442
How are you, honey?

502
00:48:14,714 --> 00:48:16,340
You're home late.

503
00:48:24,647 --> 00:48:27,180
Anyone who has anything to do
with the Monchaitrakul family

504
00:48:28,540 --> 00:48:30,940
is not allowed to set
foot in Kongpurim house.

505
00:48:37,900 --> 00:48:39,901
[Monchaitrakul]

506
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:56,776
(Next Episode) What do you think of the kid
from the Monchaitrakul family?

507
00:48:56,800 --> 00:48:59,500
Here, cream filling, as promised.

508
00:49:00,800 --> 00:49:04,500
I thought someone from the Kongpurim family
wouldn't associate with a Monchaitrakul.

509
00:49:04,600 --> 00:49:05,400
(Not pretty. Brainless.)

510
00:49:05,401 --> 00:49:08,200
Do you know who did this?
So I can get even with the right person.

511
00:49:09,500 --> 00:49:13,000
In this war between the Monchaitrakuls
and the Kongpurims... who's gonna win?

512
00:49:14,700 --> 00:49:18,200
Honestly... we shouldn't even be friends.
